The '''Deymasollians''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]]<ref name="TROS VD" /> [[Homeworld|native]] to<ref name="Planetnamia" /> the [[Colonies]]' [[Deymasoll system]].<ref name="GalaxyMap" /> They had two [[Limb|arms]] with delicate fingers and two legs&mdash;both limb pairs being relatively short<ref name="TROS VD" />&mdash;and a large [[mouth]] and prominent lower jaw.<ref name="Din">{{EncyclopediaCite|Din Djarin and Other Characters of the Underworld}}</ref> The Deymasollians had [[Color|tan]] skin, dark [[eye]]s, and a coat of white [[Hair|fur]]. All Deymasollians had keen memory,<ref name="TROS VD" /> and members of the species' society identified as belonging to at least one&mdash;female&mdash;[[gender]].<ref name="Din" />

[[Faddaff Davenspon]] was a Deymasollian who was [[Reproduction|born]]<ref name="TROS VD" /> around [[265 BBY]]. By [[35 ABY]],<ref name="265 BBY">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'', which establishes that [[Faddaff Davenspon]] was three [[Standard century|hundred years]] old, describes the state of [[the galaxy]] up to and during the events of {{Film|IX}}, which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates to [[35 ABY]].</ref> she had led a long, well-traveled life and had become an outlaw [[Technician|tech-for-hire]] specializing in [[starship]] systems, with her fingers being well-scaled for precision technology work. Davenspon had spent many [[winter]]s on the [[Mid Rim Territories]] [[planet]] [[Kijimi]], which resulted in her fur having grown thicker,<ref name="TROS VD" /> and at one point in 35 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|ABY]],<ref name="265 BBY" /> the Deymasollian was present at [[Kijimi City]]'s [[Spice Runners' Den]].<ref name="TROS">{{Film|IX}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The Deymasollian species first appeared in<ref name="TROS" /> the [[2019]] [[sequel trilogy]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']].<ref name="YearByYear">''[[Star Wars Year By Year: A Visual History, New Edition]]''</ref> [[:File:Wizard_16.png|Concept art]] of the Deymasollian Faddaff Davenspon was created for the film by creature concept designer and senior sculptor [[Louis Wiltshire]],<ref name="Art">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker]]''</ref> and the character was portrayed by<ref name="Fadden">{{WebCite|url=https://www.barbarafadden.com|text=Barbara Fadden &ndash; Creature Performer {{!}} Actress|author=[[Barbara Fadden]]|archivedate=20220404171843}}</ref> creature and droid puppeteer [[Barbara Fadden]].<ref name="TROS" /> The species was identified by name in the film's accompanying reference book ''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' by [[Pablo Hidalgo]].<ref name="TROS VD" />

